WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.169
Luffy's Devil Fruit Is The Mythical Zoan Fruit
Model Monkey King Sun Wukong.

00:00:06.169 --> 00:00:11.339
That might sound crazy, but One Piece is actually
heavily inspired by the story of Momotaro,

00:00:11.339 --> 00:00:17.689
the journey to the west and, as author Eiichrio
Oda stated himself by Akira Toriyama's Dragon

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:23.990
Ball, who's main character is called Son Goku,
which is literally the Japanese name for Sun

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:24.990
Wukong.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:29.560
And as I will show you, Monkey D. Luffy's
character and journey to become pirate king

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:35.240
clearly parallels that of the infamous Monkey
King, who rebelled against the gods before

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:43.490
finding enlightenment.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:47.340
What's up, my name is Manu and I'm not gonna
lie, I've been looking for an excuse to make

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.430
this video for a long time.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:55.610
I absolutely love any type of mythology, which
makes sense because it's basically the granddaddy

00:00:55.610 --> 00:01:03.400
of all modern fiction, ancient anime if you
like.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:08.119
And no other epic has been as influential
for the unparalleled rise of Shounen Anime

00:01:08.119 --> 00:01:13.130
throughout the world, as the so-called 'Journey
to the West', a novel published during the

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:18.750
Ming Dynasty in 16th century China, that tells
the story of the Monk Xuanzang and the Monkey

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:24.289
King Sun Wukong and their adventure to retrieve
the sacred Buddhist scripts.

00:01:24.289 --> 00:01:29.479
Not only was I surprised to find out that
Sun Wukong is actually the archetype Shounen

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:32.090
protagonist, quite literally, as I will show
you in a second, but more importantly, that

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:37.679
together with the story of Momotaro, it serves
as one of the major inspirations for One Piece

00:01:37.679 --> 00:01:48.369
and its protagonist Monkey D. Luffy.

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:52.950
And now with recent events in the story, it
seems that there is way more to luffy and

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:56.039
his powers than we originally though.

00:01:56.039 --> 00:02:00.460
As you know, I've been talking about Luffy
and his abilities quite a bit recently, speculating

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:05.909
about his awakening, the true nature of the
gomu gomu no mi and the secret behind devil

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:06.909
fruits overall.

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:11.830
But when I started combining my research on
devil fruits and One Piece's ties to mythology,

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:18.340
nothing yet has had me as excited as the idea
that Sun Wukong might be a much more literal

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.100
part of Luffy's character than I originally
thought.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:27.130
Because as I will show you, Luffy's devil
fruit might very well be the mythical zoan

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.660
fruit of Sun Wukong himself.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:34.130
So, who exactly is Sun Wukong?

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.670
Sun Wukong's name literally translates as
the “monkey awakened by the emptiness”

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:43.670
and is meant to represent his spiritual journey
from an ignorant, short-tempered monkey to

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.100
a benevolent, enlightened being.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.170
Even though he technically isn't the main
protagonist of the journey to the west, he

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.420
might as well be.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:57.480
Not only is he the most famous character of
the story, but the entire first part deals

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.900
with his origin story.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.490
The second part then introduces the Monk and
sets up the quest.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:07.660
Part three details the adventures and journey
to acquire the sacred scrolls and the last

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:12.990
chapter quickly describes the parties return
home, where both the monk and Sun Wukong reach

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.160
the status of a buddha.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:21.810
Despite being over 500 years old, the story
is filled with a mixture of humour, epic action

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:26.320
sequences and an odyssey of self-realisation
and achievements,...

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.880
... as far as I can tell at least, I don't.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:30.880
actually.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.150
speak Chinese.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:38.010
And this popular format has since become the
blueprint for story arcs within many of Shonen

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:41.710
Jump’s most popular titles.

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:48.070
Sun Wukong's story follows the exact same
arc that Jojo author Hirohiko Araki describes

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:52.890
in his book 'Manga in theory and practice'
that has been nothing short of a treasure

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.710
trove for my videos by the way.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:04:00.100
So I encourage you to try and pay attention
to how much of luffy you can recognise in

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.540
this next bit.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:06.870
Being born from a stone, similar to how Momotaro
was born from a Peach, Sun Wukong trains with

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:11.920
the other monkeys on his island before setting
out into the world, seeking new powers, learning

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:17.120
to be a leader, and even ascending to heaven
itself, where he eats the forbidden fruit

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.229
of immortality, actually.

00:04:18.229 --> 00:04:24.699
While very kind, he is also extremely careless,
eager to get stronger and fight and basically

00:04:24.699 --> 00:04:32.259
just have a good time.

00:04:32.259 --> 00:04:37.710
Feeling like nothing can possibly stop him,
he causes havoc with the gods, who cant seem

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:43.539
to stop him until the Buddha himself steps
in, who seals him under a rock.

00:04:43.539 --> 00:04:48.199
To grow as a person, he is then sent on his
journey with the Monk and two other demon

00:04:48.199 --> 00:04:53.440
comrades, which is grouped into a number of
arcs, very similar to what we know from shounen

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.440
anime.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:05:00.180
The monkey king goes through a lot of change
throughout, acquiring new and stronger abilities,

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:06.020
fighting the forces of heaven and being utterly
defeated, finding loyal companions, and ultimately

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:13.529
achieving greatness.

00:05:13.529 --> 00:05:20.260
His godly powers include superhuman strength,
speed and the ability to transform into 72

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:21.460
different forms.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:27.650
He also wields a magic pole that can be stretched
and shrunken and magical cloud he can ride

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.150
through the heavens.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:35.060
And even when facing seemingly unbeatable
opponents, Sun Wukong always displays a certain

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:40.260
playfulness, enjoying fighting against worthy
opponents and quickly becomes known throughout

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:41.630
the demon world.

